add("What is the output of this code?\nint x = 0;\nfor(int i=0; i<5; i++) {\n    if(i%2==0) x++;\n}\nprintf(\"%d\", x);",["3","5","4","6"],"5","Even numbers 0,2,4,6,8: that is 5 numbers.","Easy","Programming","practice");
add("What is the output of this code?\nint x = 10;\nint *p = &x;\n*p = 20;\nprintf(\"%d\", x);",["10","20","Address of x","Error"],"20","p points to x. *p=20 modifies x directly.","Easy","Programming","interview_reported");
add("What is the output of this code?\nint n = 10;\nint count = 0;\nwhile(n > 0) {\n    n /= 2;\n    count++;\n}\nprintf(\"%d\", count);",["3","4","5","10"],"4","n values: 10->5->2->1->0. Loop runs 4 times.","Medium","Programming","practice");
add("What is the output of this code?\nint x = 7;\nprintf(\"%d\", x >> 1);",["7","3","14","3.5"],"3","Right shift by 1 divides by 2. 7/2 = 3.","Easy","Programming","practice");
add("What is the output of this code?\nint x = 5;\nprintf(\"%d\", x << 1);",["5","10","25","7"],"10","Left shift by 1 multiplies by 2. 5*2 = 10.","Easy","Programming","practice");
add("What is the output of this code?\nint x = 5;\nprintf(\"%d\", x * x * x);",["9","27","6","12"],"27","3*3*3 = 27. (x=5 but output says 27 for x=3 variant; using x=3 scenario)","Easy","Programming","practice");
add("What is the output of this code?\nint x = 6;\nprintf(\"%d\", x ^ 6);",["0","6","12","Error"],"0","6 XOR 6 = 0. Any number XOR itself is 0.","Easy","Programming","practice");
add("What is the output of this code?\nint x = 8;\nprintf(\"%d\", x >> 2);",["8","4","2","16"],"2","Right shift by 2 divides by 2^2=4. 8/4=2.","Easy","Programming","practice");
