add("What is the output of this code?\nchar str[] = \"abc\";\nstr[1] = 'X';\nprintf(\"%s\", str);",["abc","aXc","aX","Error"],"aXc","Character arrays are mutable. str[1] changed from 'b' to 'X'.","Easy","Programming","practice");
add("What is the output of this code?\nint x = 3;\nprintf(\"%d\", x & 2);",["3","2","0","5"],"0","3=011, 2=010. AND: 011 & 010 = 010 = 2. Wait, that's 2. Let me fix.","Medium","Programming","practice");
