add("What is the output of this Java code?\nclass A { { System.out.print(\"Init\"); } }\nnew A();",["Init","Compilation error","Runtime error","Nothing"],"Init","Instance initializer block runs when an object is created, before the constructor.","Medium","OOP","practice");
add("What is the output?\nclass Test { Test() { System.out.print(\"T\"); } }\nTest t1 = new Test();\nTest t2 = new Test();",["TT","T","TTT","Error"],"TT","Each new Test() calls the constructor. Two objects = two constructor calls.","Easy","OOP","practice");
add("What is the difference between 'this' and 'super' in Java?",["this refers to current object; super refers to parent object","They are the same","this is static; super is instance","super is used only in interfaces"],"this refers to current object; super refers to parent object","this accesses current class members; super accesses parent class members.","Easy","OOP","practice");
add("What is the output of this code?\nclass Parent { void show() { System.out.println(\"Parent\"); } }\nclass Child extends Parent { void show() { System.out.println(\"Child\"); } }\nParent p = new Child();\np.show();",["Parent","Child","Compilation error","Runtime error"],"Child","Method overriding: runtime type determines which method is called.","Easy","OOP","interview_reported");
